#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store Qiskit objects to disk so you can continue where you left off"
msgstr ""
"Stocke des objets Qiskit sur disque pour reprendre là où tu t'étais arrêté"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save circuits to disk"
msgstr "Sauvegarder des circuits sur disque"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versions des packages\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le code de cette page a été développé avec les prérequis suivants.\n"
"Nous recommandons d'utiliser ces versions ou des versions plus récentes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use [QPY serialization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) to save your circuit to file. QPY files store the full Qiskit circuit object and will be compatible with newer versions of Qiskit (although not necessarily with older versions of Qiskit).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Utilise la [sérialisation QPY](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) pour sauvegarder ton circuit dans un fichier. Les fichiers QPY stockent l'objet circuit Qiskit complet et seront compatibles avec les versions plus récentes de Qiskit (mais pas nécessairement avec les versions plus anciennes).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "To demonstrate, the following cell creates a simple quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour illustrer cela, la cellule suivante crée un circuit quantique simple.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To save this file to disk, use the `qpy.dump` function. You can also save a "
"list of circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour sauvegarder ce fichier sur disque, utilise la fonction `qpy.dump`. Tu "
"peux également sauvegarder une liste de circuits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This circuit is now saved to the file `test.qpy`. If you restart your Python"
" kernel, you can re-load the circuit using the `qpy.load` function. Note "
"that this always returns a list of circuits, even if you only serialized one"
" circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ce circuit est maintenant sauvegardé dans le fichier `test.qpy`. Si tu "
"redémarres ton noyau Python, tu peux recharger le circuit à l'aide de la "
"fonction `qpy.load`. Note que cette fonction retourne toujours une liste de "
"circuits, même si tu n'en as sérialisé qu'un seul.\n"

